cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FFIEC AI Chain-of-Custody &mdash; Proposed Standard"
message: "If you reference this specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Muchow
    given-names: Steven
    email: smuchow1962@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/smuchow1962/ffiec-chain-of-custody"
url: "https://github.com/smuchow1962/ffiec-chain-of-custody"
abstract: >
  A proposed open standard for tamper-evident logging of AI-driven decisions
  in regulated financial institutions. Defines a four-primitive chain of
  custody (per-event HMAC chain, daily Merkle seal, HSM-rooted root signature,
  OpenTelemetry-native wire) designed to satisfy the integrity-of-logging
  requirements in the FFIEC IT Examination Handbook (Information Security
  and Architecture, Infrastructure, and Operations booklets) and related
  model-risk-management guidance (SR 26-2, OCC Bulletin 2026-13). Currently
  Public Review Draft 1 (PRD-1).
keywords:
  - FFIEC
  - chain of custody
  - AI audit
  - model risk management
  - tamper-evident logging
  - Merkle seal
  - HMAC
  - HSM
  - OpenTelemetry
  - banking regulation
